. * we specify a twoway-fixed effects model using hhworkhours as a proxy for ge
> nder egalitarian hhwork as DV and an interaction of having the first daugther
>  (time-varying) dummy and gender as IV assuming that on average, females do m
> ore household work than males as shown by past research (e.g., Nitsche & Grun
> ow, 2016); we would therefore expect that the effect of transitioning into ha
> ving a daughter on hours spent with household work is more positive for males
>  than for females.
